DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ppiijjuuiiccee driver provides support for the PiJuice HAT, an uninterrupt‐
     ible power supply for the Raspberry Pi.  The integrated STM32F030CCT6 mi‐
     cro controller provides access through the I2C bus to several battery
     status values.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     iic(4), intro(4), maxrtc(4), apm(8), sysctl(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ppiijjuuiiccee driver first appeared in OpenBSD 7.3.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
     The ppiijjuuiiccee driver was written by Marcus Glocker <_m_g_l_o_c_k_e_r_@_o_p_e_n_b_s_d_._o_r_g>.

CCAAVVEEAATTSS
     The PiJuice HAT EEPROM currently doesn't contain the device tree informa‐
     tion to match and attach this device.  It requires a custom device tree
     blob overlay which gets loaded during the bootstrapping process.

